  "notes": "A drawn-out vocalization showing that the speaker is thinking, hesitating, or reluctant. The long vowel signals that an answer is not coming immediately.\n\nTYPICAL USES:\n- Buying time to think before answering\n- Expressing mild doubt or reluctance ('well, I'm not sure...')\n- Reacting to something troubling or hard to decide\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- うん: yeah, mm — short; a casual 'yes' or simple acknowledgment\n- えーと: um, let me see — filler used while searching for words",
